xquest (1.3-3) unstable; urgency=low

  * Demo recording, playback and attract mode, in the original .dmo format.
  * Settings and high scores persist in ~/.config/xquest.
  * Wall collision is now pixel-accurate, matching the original; the port
    was killing players on grazes the original forgave.
  * Closing the window during a game now quits instead of returning to
    the menu.

 -- David <david@katalystnord.com>  Sat, 29 Aug 2026 20:55:00 +0200

xquest (1.3-2) unstable; urgency=low

  * Menu mouse support: hover to highlight, click to activate, scroll wheel
    to cycle items.

 -- David <david@katalystnord.com>  Mon, 30 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0200

xquest (1.3-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Initial Debian packaging of the SDL2 port.
  * Faithful port of XQuest v1.3 (DOS, 1994) to Linux/SDL2:
    - 18 enemy types with AI, collision, and scoring
    - 8-channel PCM audio mixer (xquest.snd, 11025 Hz mono)
    - High-score table (xquest.scr binary format)
    - 3-D starfield background, animated title screen
    - Full keyboard/mouse/joystick input
    - Wall-contact destruction (Timid+ difficulty)

 -- David <david@katalystnord.com>  Thu, 11 Jun 2026 18:18:40 +0200
